course: dictionary
lesson: 15404
title: A true sportsman
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sportsman is a person who plays sport, often very well or as their job. «The sportsman scored three goals in the final.» The clues are sport and goals, so a sportsman is someone who plays a sport.
explain: The word can also praise how someone plays. «Even after losing, Maya shook hands with the winners. She is a true sportsman.» Maya is not praised for winning. She is praised for playing fairly, being polite and taking defeat well.
explain: To check, swap in another phrase and see if the sentence still makes sense. «Ben kicked the ball out to let the injured boy get treatment.» Kicking the ball out is fair play, not just playing a game, so this is a sportsman's behaviour.
fact: A sportsman is a man who plays sport, especially well or as his job.
fact: A sportsman also plays fairly, is polite to the other side, and accepts losing well.
fact: The quality of fair play is called sportsmanship.
fact: Common phrases are «a good sportsman», «sportsman of the year» and «a true sportsman».
fact: An older meaning is a man who goes hunting, shooting or fishing for sport.
exercise: «The sportsman scored three goals in the final.» What is a sportsman? | A person who sells sports clothes | A referee who blows the whistle | *A man who plays sport, especially well or as his job | A coach who shouts from the side
exercise: «Even after losing, Maya shook hands with the winners. She is a true sportsman.» What is this sentence praising? | *Her fair play and polite behaviour, even in defeat | Her high score | Her loud voice at the match | Her new trainers
exercise: Which word names the quality of playing fairly and taking defeat well? | *sportsmanship | sportswear | sporty | sports day
test: «The team captain was a true sportsman, helping the other side up after a fall.» What does this story praise? | Winning every match | Wearing the best kit | *Fair play and kindness to the other side | Running the fastest
test: In the older sense, «The sportsman sat quietly by the lake with his rod, waiting for a fish.» What is he doing? | Reading the sports pages | Cooking dinner | *Fishing for sport | Playing a football match
exam: «The sportsman accepted defeat with a smile and congratulated the winners.» Which word best describes him? | Cheat | Lazy | *Sportsman, showing good sportsmanship | Stranger
